    "headline": "Red Flag Warning issued October 15 at 2:02PM PDT until October 16 at 11:00AM PDT by NWS Eureka CA",
    "description": "* AFFECTED AREA...Fire weather zones 418 including Lake Pillsbury,\n419 including the City of Clearlake, Middletown, Lower Lake, and\nIndian Valley Reservoir, and 420 including Cobb and Mount\nKonocti.\n\n* WIND...Sustained winds of 15 to 25mph with gusts to 35 mph\npossible in exposed areas.\n\n* HUMIDITY...Low overnight recoveries of 30-35% will drop to\n10- 20% through the morning. Very poor RH recovery into\nFriday.\n\n* IMPACTS...any fires that develop will likely spread rapidly.",
    "instruction": "A Red Flag Warning means that critical fire weather conditions\nare either occurring now, or will shortly. A combination of\nstrong winds, low relative humidity, and warm temperatures can\ncontribute to extreme fire behavior.",
